# Emeritus Prime Bank 

Hey there! Welcome to the Emeritus Prime Bank demo. I built this project as a self-contained, front-end UI experiment. As a final-year Application Development student, I'm constantly bridging the gap between theory and practical coding. I wanted a sandbox project to really get my hands dirty with React and modern build tools like Vite, and this is the result.

**A quick disclaimer:** This is entirely a front-end "smoke and mirrors" demo. There is no backend, no database, and definitely no real money involved. That "face scan" button? Just a fun animation I managed to figure out! Everything resets the moment you reload the page.

## Why I Built This

Between juggling my final-year modules and figuring out the architectural side of things, I wanted to prove to myself that I could build an interface that actually *looks* and *feels* production-ready. It's been an awesome learning curve-figuring out how to structure components cleanly, manage state without a real backend, and keep the user experience smooth. I'm still growing as a dev, but this project was a huge step in piecing the puzzle together.

