## Want to run it locally?

If you want to clone this and play around with the code yourself, here is how I set it up:

1. **Clone or Unzip** the project to your local machine.
2. Open it up in your favorite IDE (I use IntelliJ IDEA).
3. Open your terminal in the project root and install the dependencies:
 
   npm install

4. Fire up the development server:
   
   npm run dev

5. Click the `http://localhost:5173` link in the terminal to see it live in your browser.

## A Note for Other Devs

If you fork this, please keep the demo banner and the "simulated" warnings in place. The goal was to make it look real, which means we have a responsibility to make sure nobody actually mistakes it for a real bank!

Also, the passcode is intentionally just `1234`. Remember, I'm focusing on the UI/UX here—building iron-clad security architecture is a project for another day!
